    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fb5625b_a97800dd",
        "filename": "src/core/SkPipelineData.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-17T19:54:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ooh, I didn\u0027t notice that. I feel like a `peek` function should really not be mutating the data at all. That violates my expectations pretty significantly vs what a function named `peek` ought to do.\n\nCan we do the padding-up elsewhere, or make a dedicated function for it?",
      "parentUuid": "5d5c6dd2_c043580d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7cc2f8148d500cf8d31a2d517adb91f7e8046f4f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5fd94037_99e89cf1",
        "filename": "src/core/SkPipelineData.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T14:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d rather just rename this function, since we don\u0027t anticipate a use-case that doesn\u0027t need the padding. Would `read` be better? Any other suggestions?",
      "parentUuid": "1fb5625b_a97800dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7cc2f8148d500cf8d31a2d517adb91f7e8046f4f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
