        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T14:48:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m also in favor of just renaming it. The only time we peek it\u0027s data is when we\u0027re done writing, so maybe something like `finishUniformDataBlock()`?",
      "parentUuid": "5fd94037_99e89cf1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7cc2f8148d500cf8d31a2d517adb91f7e8046f4f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0cafd950_d1b79b94",
        "filename": "src/core/SkPipelineData.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T15:17:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think a non-const `finishUniformDataBlock()` is a great idea. That names makes it obvious that it\u0027s potentially mutating and that you shouldn\u0027t call it early. \n\nI would advocate for keeping around the const `peekUniformMethod` method as-is, just doing what a peek should do (show me the data as-is, no mutations or funny business) even if it\u0027s only really useful for testing. The last line of `finishUniformDataBlock()` could be `return this-\u003epeekUniformData()`.",
      "parentUuid": "72582e18_37cead8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7cc2f8148d500cf8d31a2d517adb91f7e8046f4f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a7d5ca4_1795ab7c",
        "filename": "src/core/SkPipelineData.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T15:26:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like having both would be confusing. If we assume that when you operate on an SkUniformDataBlock, you get the aligned, safe data, then you could get tripped up depending on how you got the SkUniformDataBlock (was it returnedby finishUniformDataBlock, or peekUniformData?)\n\nRight now there\u0027s some important memory reuse optimizations in the tight loop of preparing the DrawPass in graphite that accumulates each draw\u0027s data, and that ought to remain the sole/primary place this gets called in \"real\" code. I think test can work just fine with padding being added, and we just update their expectations like James did for this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "0cafd950_d1b79b94",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7cc2f8148d500cf8d31a2d517adb91f7e8046f4f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
